{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Judah went down.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: he went down from his greatness because of the sale [of Joseph]. And Rabbi Abraham of blessed memory raised the difficulty: from the sale until they went down to Egypt you find only twenty-two years, for Joseph at the time of his sale was seventeen years old, and at standing before Pharaoh he was thirty — that is thirteen years from the sale until then, and seven of plenty and two of famine, thus twenty-two years, and in that same year they went down to Egypt. From when Judah married the daughter of a Canaanite man until they went down to Egypt, you will find more — for count one year for the birth of Er, one year for the birth of Onan, [and one year for the birth of Shelah] — that is three years, and it is written ״כי ראתה כי גדל שלה,״ which implies he was thirteen years old — that is sixteen years; for the birth of Peretz, that is seventeen. And even if you say that Peretz was only seven years old when he begat Hetzron, and one year for the birth of Chamul, who was among those who went down to Egypt — in any case you will find twenty-five years. Thus this 'went down' is before the sale. And one may answer: this ״כי גדל שלה״ was stated regarding the matter of intercourse, for he was already nine years old. As we learned in tractate Nedarim: a boy of nine years and one day who has intercourse with his yevamah acquires her. And we say in Sanhedrin that the early ones would father children at seven years."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:39.346219533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}